WEBVTT

00:00.113 --> 00:14.221
render-configs renders one config file per service, on a pool with room for four at a time.

00:14.221 --> 00:22.196
The pool is full, so the other items wait for capacity. The note above the graph says why.

00:22.196 --> 00:39.897
The card beside the tasks says what it waits for: every cpu of pool batch is reserved, by the items that are running.

00:39.897 --> 00:48.064
An item finishes and frees its reservation, and a waiting item starts at once.

00:48.064 --> 00:51.283
Nothing was retried and nothing was lost: each item waited for room, then ran.
